I'm not trying to be obnoxious here, I'm just trying to establish
whether there's actually a _problem_ in the code, or whether there's
just a potential inconsistency that future developers/patchers should be
aware of... ie. that NOHANDS doesn't necessarily cover all the things
that you'd think would have no hands, so be careful when you use it.

For example, a quick grep indicates that most of the time, it's being
applied to youmonst.data -- in other words, it's checking to see if the
player's (potentially polymorphed) form has hands, and thus whether the
player can take a particular action.  It's possible that it was _always_
intended to be player-specific.

(There's also a bug related to this, I believe, related to being able to
throw things up in the air while you're polymorphed... so if there are
any inconsistencies here, it's likely that they're already addressed in
the vanilla branch.)

